---
// The privacy notice, linked from the footer of every page beside Disclaimer and
// Cookies: what Good Call keeps, where, and who can see it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Good Call keeps your answers and data: on your device, not shared and not recorded, unless you are registered through an institution on our education plan."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <div class="longform">
    <section class="prose" id="privacy" aria-label="Your privacy">
      <p>
        You do not need an account to use Good Call. Your name, character, answers, points, time spent, the habits you
        plan and your reading settings are saved on this device only, in your browser's storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not share your data or keep a record of it. Your answers are never used to build a profile of you, so
        they cannot be used to assess you, rank you, target you or discriminate against you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only exception is if you are registered through an institution on our education plan for schools,
        colleges and NGOs. Your institution can tell you what is shared with it and why.
      </p>
      <p>
        Calendar reminders are made on your device and handed straight to your own calendar app. Good Call never sees
        your calendar and does not send you anything.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your first answer to each scenario is the one that counts, so it cannot be changed. To remove your answers from
        one course, use "Clear my answers and start again" at the end of it. To remove everything, use "Delete all my
        Good Call data" on your profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every item Good Call saves in your browser is listed on the <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> page, where you can
        also clear them.
      </p>
    </section>
    <p class="fine">What Good Call is for, and what it is not, is in the <a href={href('/disclaimer/')}>disclaimer</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
